  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: scVI with multi-profile and avgpool (config_005, acc 0.650) is the best RNA-only configuration so far, and multi-profile + avgpool is the dominant setting. However, scGPT has not been tested at all, and the RNA encoder choice is a fundamental representation decision that will govern all downstream multimodal experiments. Question: config_008 (scGPT, multi-profile, avgpool) directly isolates the encoder variable against config_005 (scVI, multi-profile, avgpool), keeping profile setting and aggregation identical. This clean single-variable comparison will reveal whether scGPT's pretrained generative representation outperforms scVI's latent representation for this task. Why this is the best next step: (1) If scGPT is substantially better, it reshapes the entire multimodal search toward scGPT-based configs; if similar or worse, we can confidently lock in scVI and pivot to testing multimodal fusion or stronger image encoders. (2) It avoids the risk of prematurely investing in multimodal configs (which add two more variables: image encoder and fusion strategy) before establishing the best RNA backbone. (3) It is the highest-information experiment available: the result constrains the design of all remaining scGPT and scVI multimodal configurations, making the most of a limited budget."
}

